        "sha256": "5ffa911fd9b6356f204646003fb9342e341810dcdfdf5cb15756e7f01ec5f770",
        "page": 31
      },
      "excerpt": "In the first test, a steady flame was established over a \n100-µm sample. After the flame propagated across half the sample length at a steady spread rate of \n2.2 mm/s, the flow was abruptly cut off and the flame was observed to extinguish within 2 s. To pin down \nthe extinction flow velocity, a second test was done under the same conditions except the flow velocity \nwas set at 3 cm/s and after the flame propagated about half the sample length, the flow was gradually \nreduced. The flame spread rate of the leading edge, as plotted in Figure 2.8, shows that the flame \nextinguishes at about 30 s after ignition. The fan voltage at that time indicates a flow velocity of about \n1.1 cm/s."
    },
    {
      "id": "PSI-25:pdf:6924805f7f6aa6a83021067c:v2:p29#a1bd2d0c9ce0",
